{"type":"assistant","uuid":"1c274dca-3fb1-433f-8ac2-2b86cfaff188","session_id":"bdb9ccf8-86f3-4a57-be15-dca19e200c70","parent_tool_use_id":null,"message":{"id":"1c274dca-3fb1-433f-8ac2-2b86cfaff188","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen/qwen3.6-35b-a3b","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Bug fixed.** Here's a summary:\n\n**Root cause:** In `ESPFragment.java`, the `doInBackground` method constructs a URL from user input without validating the host. When the user enters an invalid host like `.lo`, the string `\"http://.lo\"` is passed to OkHttp's `Request.Builder.url()`, which throws `IllegalArgumentException`. The original code only caught `IOException`, leaving this exception unhandled — causing the app to crash.\n\n**Fix:** Changed the catch clause from `catch (IOException e)` to `catch (IOException | IllegalArgumentException e)`. This catches the `IllegalArgumentException` thrown by OkHttp when the URL host is invalid, prevents the crash, and allows `onPostExecute` to show the existing \"Please enter valid IP address\" error message to the user instead."}],"stop_reason":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":23145,"output_tokens":180,"cache_read_input_tokens":21120,"total_tokens":23325}}}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","uuid":"a0470d97-71a1-4b29-8dff-035cfe7a72a5","session_id":"bdb9ccf8-86f3-4a57-be15-dca19e200c70","is_error":false,"duration_ms":79957,"duration_api_ms":29821,"num_turns":7,"result":"**Bug fixed.** Here's a summary:\n\n**Root cause:** In `ESPFragment.java`, the `doInBackground` method constructs a URL from user input without validating the host. When the user enters an invalid host like `.lo`, the string `\"http://.lo\"` is passed to OkHttp's `Request.Builder.url()`, which throws `IllegalArgumentException`. The original code only caught `IOException`, leaving this exception unhandled — causing the app to crash.\n\n**Fix:** Changed the catch clause from `catch (IOException e)` to `catch (IOException | IllegalArgumentException e)`. This catches the `IllegalArgumentException` thrown by OkHttp when the URL host is invalid, prevents the crash, and allows `onPostExecute` to show the existing \"Please enter valid IP address\" error message to the user instead.","usage":{"input_tokens":147627,"output_tokens":1933,"cache_read_input_tokens":115104,"total_tokens":149560},"permission_denials":[]}
